<title>FINLAND: HANDELSBANKEN SEES RISK OF MARKKA APPRECIATION.</title>
<headline>HANDELSBANKEN SEES RISK OF MARKKA APPRECIATION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Handelsbanken said in a statement received on Friday that it saw a risk of appreciation pressures on the markka.</p>
<p>&quot;A pressure for the markka to appreciate may appear. That would be met by massive interventions from the Bank of Finland to keep the markka within the ERM band,&quot; Handelsbanken said, adding interventions would boost currency reserves.</p>
<p>It expected the central bank to target a fluctuation in the ERM of 2.25 percent up or down and Finnish short-term interest rates to move in &quot;perfect correlation&quot; with their German equivalents.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
